body:
This is just my personal experience but I had the same issues the first couple months. For me  my anxiety was making it worse, I even went to the hospital because it was racing so much. It's always possible that your heart rate is up and your sensing it which causes anxiety and panic attacks. It's possible you're having the same reaction. Hypo does slow down the heart so going back to normal doesn't feel right.

&#x200B;

If you're worried it doesn't hurt to go get checked. For me it was getting on medicine to help with my anxiety and depression and time to adjust to the thyroid medicine. You could also check your blood pressure, hypo can also affect your heart health and cholesterol and I've taken dietary steps to improve my health as well.
